    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nHere's a reproduceable case which I think also describes the problem:\n \n- In a Markdown document type \\`hello , at this point if you type another \\` it will insert (2) \\`\\` instead of just (1) \\` leaving you with \\`hello\\`\\`\n  - Under normal cases if you type \\` by itself it will insert \\`\\` so you can put your contents in between that but there's been dozens of cases where I ended up in a scenario where I had \\`hello\\`\\` but wanted \\`hello\\`\n- Assorted cases with ' and \"\" where I ended up with \"hello\"\" instead of \"hello\" based on the same issue as above with Markdown\n  - This feels like it could be a fundamental behavior that affects all pairs\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\nCheck above.",
