            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hi, the description mentions that but here's a sequence with the default config:\n\n1. Insert this text into a Markdown file:\n\n```\nHello world\n```\n\n2. Put your cursor where the `|` is:\n\n```\nHello |world\n```\n\n3. Enter in \\`, at this point `mini.pairs` will change the text to:\n\n```\nHello `|world\n```\n\n4. Put your cursor where the `|` is:\n\n```\nHello `world|\n```\n\n5. Enter in \\`, at this point `mini.pairs` will change the text to this and put the cursor in the middle:\n\n```\nHello `world`|`\n```\n\nStep 5 is the problem. It should be:\n\n```\nHello `world`|\n```\n\nThis can be repeated with quotes and I'm guessing other characters too.",
