            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> By the way, https://github.com/windwp/nvim-autopairs will produce step 5 with the expected outcome (at least IMO). I just thought I'd add this context so you know why some folks might choose to switch to nvim-autopairs.\n\nYeah, I know, and there is no problem with not using 'mini.pairs'. Although it works perfectly with less overhead in the use cases it is designed for.\n\n> I use `mini.ai` when I can but when naturally typing sometimes it's easier to manually add the quotes or character.\n\nTyping `saiw'` to surround a word with quotes is arguably easier than `i<C-v>'<Esc>ea<C-v>'<Esc>` (`<C-v>` are needed to actually insert a single character), that's why it is the recommended approach here.",
