            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Then go back to world and put in the ` before the \"w\" ...\n\nThat inserts the pair ``` `` ``` with default 'mini.pairs' config.\n\n> ... but what happens when you have a few words such as:\n> \n> ```\n> Hello world this is a sentence\n> ```\n> And now you want \"this is a sentence\" to be wrapped in quotes. You have to go back to using a visual selection right?\n\nIn this particular case it is \"put cursor on start of `this`\" and type `sa$'` to surround from cursor until the end of line.\n\nAnd yes, in a more complex cases it is always possible to visually select and type `sa'`. To make it even more straightforward, there are several \"smart jump plugins\" that allow to jump to arbitrary locations and which work for both visual selection (Visual mode) and as operator target (Operator-pending mode). Both 'mini.jump' and 'mini.jump2d' are among them.",
